# Docker build-context ignore (TASK-270).
#
# The build context for all three images is the monorepo ROOT (npm workspaces),
# so a single root-level .dockerignore is correct — Docker only honors one, at
# the context root. Everything the image needs (workspace manifests, source,
# prisma schema, next configs, public assets, packages/*) is installed/built
# INSIDE the image, so host build output and dependencies are excluded to keep
# the context small and to guarantee no host secrets ever enter an image layer.

# ─── Dependencies & build output (rebuilt in the image) ─────────────────────
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/build
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/.swc

# ─── Secrets — never bake any env file into a build context ──────────────────
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ─── Local dev uploads — must not leak into an image layer (a named volume
#     provides these at runtime, see docker-compose.prod.yml) ────────────────
apps/store-api/uploads
apps/store-*/uploads

# ─── VCS / tooling / editor noise ───────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store

# ─── Tests, docs & CI artifacts not needed to build a runnable image ────────
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts
**/*.int-spec.ts
**/__tests__
**/__mocks__
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.playwright
docs
requirements.md
BACKLOG.md

# ─── Docker / compose files themselves ──────────────────────────────────────
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
Caddyfile
